  "assumptions": [
    "Illustration: a made-up two-setting loss bowl with simulated batch noise, not a real model trained on real data.",
    "Loss = (2.5 x^2 + 0.5 z^2) / 2, steeper along x, drawn at 0.5 times the loss. Without noise, the ball overshoots in x when learning rate > 0.4 and diverges when it is above 0.8.",
    "Each step = -learning rate x (true slope + noise). Noise sd = 1.5 x sqrt((64 - B) / (63 B)) per direction: 1.5 at B = 1, exactly 0 at B = 64 (the whole simulated set).",
    "Both arrows are drawn at true length (scale 1): orange is the next mini-batch step, the way the ball will move; grey is the full-data step, -learning rate x true slope.",
    "A run ends after 40 steps (finished) or when the loss exceeds 12 (diverged). The trail holds the start plus up to 40 steps. Noise comes from a fixed sequence, so Reset replays it.",
    "The ball moves one step every 4 host ticks (about 7.5 steps per second at speed 1). Far-off positions are capped at the bowl's edge on screen; the Loss readout keeps the true value."
  ],
  "program": {
    "source": "const A=2.5,C=0.5,K=0.5,R=0.12,N=40,LIM=12,ST=[1.5,1.7];\nconst L=(x,z)=>0.5*(A*x*x+C*z*z);\nconst rnd=n=>{const s=Math.sin(n*12.9898+78.233)*43758.5453;return s-Math.floor(s);};\nconst gs=n=>Math.sqrt(-2*Math.log(Math.max(1e-9,rnd(n))))*Math.cos(2*Math.PI*rnd(n+0.37));\nconst sd=b=>1.5*Math.sqrt(Math.max(0,64-b)/(63*b));\nconst nxt=(s,i)=>{const d=sd(Number(i.batchSize)),k=s.run*997+s.step*3+1,lr=i.learningRate;return[-lr*(A*s.x+d*gs(k)),-lr*(C*s.z+d*gs(k+1.5))];};\nconst done=s=>s.div||s.step>=N;\nconst word=s=>s.div?'diverged':s.step>=N?'finished':'running';\nfunction adv(s,i){if(done(s))return s;const[dx,dz]=nxt(s,i),x=s.x+dx,z=s.z+dz;return{...s,x,z,step:s.step+1,div:L(x,z)>LIM,path:s.path.concat([[x,z]])};}\nconst fresh=(run,kept)=>({x:ST[0],z:ST[1],step:0,run,div:false,path:[ST],kept});\nexport function initialState(){return fresh(0,[]);}\nexport function reduce({state:s,event:e,inputs}){\nif(e.type==='step')return e.tick%4?s:adv(s,inputs);\nif(e.type==='action'&&e.action==='newRun')return fresh(s.run+1,s.step>0?s.path:s.kept);\nreturn s;}\nconst cl=v=>Math.max(-2.2,Math.min(2.2,v));\nconst lift=p=>{const x=cl(p[0]),z=cl(p[1]);return[x,Math.min(K*L(x,z),3.2)+0.05,z];};\nfunction aim(dx,dz,on){const l=Math.hypot(dx,dz),h=Math.SQRT1_2;return on&&l>1e-6?{visible:true,quaternion:[dz/l*h,0,-dx/l*h,h],scale:[1,l,1]}:{visible:false};}\nexport function evaluate({inputs,state}){\nconst s=state||initialState(),live=!done(s),[dx,dz]=nxt(s,inputs),lr=inputs.learningRate,b=lift([s.x,s.z]);\nreturn{nodes:{ball:{position:[b[0],b[1]-0.05+R,b[2]]},stepArrow:aim(dx,dz,live),trueArrow:aim(-lr*A*s.x,-lr*C*s.z,live&&inputs.showTrueGradient),trail:{points:s.path.map(lift)},ghost:{points:s.kept.map(lift)}},\nreadouts:{loss:L(s.x,s.z),steps:s.step,stepLen:live?Math.hypot(dx,dz):0,status:word(s)}};}\n"
  }
}